{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "ee164a1a-32c0-5adf-b341-fe20e94f7608",
  "Description": "A wall of 80 bricks from one brick geometry, knocked down by a heavy block.\n\nOne [CubeGeometry] is the brick: connected to the Geometry input of [RigidBody] it is the collider, and [GridPoints] through the Points input makes one body per point. [RigidBodyGeometry] returns the simulated bricks as geometry, which [GeometryToMesh] compiles for drawing. The brick is described once. The projectile is a primitive [RigidBody] with no geometry at all; [RigidBodyGeometry] gives it a box of its own size.\n\nAKA: pyramid, colosseum, stack, instances, bodies from points, geometry\n\nTips\n- Change Size on the [CubeGeometry] and both the collider and the drawing follow.\n- Change the counts on [GridPoints] to build a bigger wall; no other node changes.\n- Set Reset on [PhysicsWorld] to rebuild the wall.",
